1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:04,527
The biggest soda lake on Earth is hiding in Türkiye.

2
00:00:04,807 --> 00:00:09,018
And beneath its surface, there are towers that nobody built.

3
00:00:09,468 --> 00:00:12,623
This is Lake Van, in eastern Türkiye,

4
00:00:12,903 --> 00:00:17,055
sitting about one thousand six hundred forty metres above sea level.

5
00:00:17,335 --> 00:00:19,552
It's the largest lake in the country.

6
00:00:20,002 --> 00:00:23,864
Rivers flow in, but nothing flows out.

7
00:00:24,144 --> 00:00:29,505
Water only leaves by evaporating, so the lake turns strongly alkaline,

8
00:00:29,785 --> 00:00:32,818
with a pH of about nine point eight.

9
00:00:34,568 --> 00:00:40,774
And deep below, bacteria built stone towers up to forty metres tall,

10
00:00:41,054 --> 00:00:43,802
the largest of their kind ever found.

11
00:00:44,252 --> 00:00:46,791
Its mud keeps a diary, too.

12
00:00:47,071 --> 00:00:52,844
Layer by layer, it records six hundred thousand years of climate.

13
00:00:53,294 --> 00:00:58,355
A lake that is a laboratory, a museum and a diary.

14
00:00:58,635 --> 00:00:59,975
What else is it hiding?
